\
StartFragmentArmenian soprano Anna Avdalyan has been a permanent \
ensemble member of the Schleswig-Holsteinisches \
Landestheater since January 2023. From an early age, she \
gained stage experience through concert tours and regular \
performances, developing a strong connection to music and \
singing during her childhood. \
At the age of 18, she became a permanent member of the \
professional State Chamber Choir of Armenia, under the \
direction of Robert Mlqeyan. In 2015, she also appeared \
as a soloist with the choir Our Lady of Armenia at St Peter’s \
Basilica in Rome, performing before Pope Francis. \
Her vocal studies brought her to Germany, where she \
attended the Stuttgart University of Music and \
Performing Arts, studying with Professor Ulrike \
Sonntag. She graduated with distinction with a Bachelor’s \
degree in Voice in 2019 and continued her training in the \
Master’s programme in Opera, completing her studies in \
2022. \
During her studies in Stuttgart, Anna Avdalyan was also \
active as a concert soloist. Her musical repertoire includes \
works from the oratorio and concert repertoire, as well as \
art song. These include works by Mozart, Bach and Orff. \
While still a student, Anna Avdalyan gained her first \
professional stage experience at several German theatres. \
Her early engagements included the Schleswig\
Holsteinisches Landestheater, Theater Görlitz-Zittau and \
the Bavarian State Opera in Munich, where she appeared as \
Ursuline in Krzysztof Penderecki’s The Devils of Loudun. \
In Görlitz, she performed roles including Anna in Der liebe \
Augustin, Mimi in Prinz von Preußen and Papagena and the \
Queen of the Night in Mozart’s The Magic Flute. Following \
a permanent engagement at Theater Görlitz-Zittau, she \
continued her artistic career in Flensburg. \
At the Schleswig-Holsteinisches Landestheater, she has \
developed a varied repertoire spanning opera, operetta and \
musical theatre. Her roles there include Molly in One Touch \
of Venus, Susanna in Mozart’s Le nozze di Figaro, \
Constance in Poulenc’s Dialogues des Carmélites and \
Mabel in Gilbert and Sullivan’s The Pirates of Penzance. In \
the musical production of Jekyll & Hyde, she performed the \
role of Lisa. \
Alongside her operatic work, she continues to perform in \
concert programmes. \
Anna Avdalyan combines her work on the opera stage with \
a diverse concert career. Her artistic profile brings together \
the agility and brilliance of coloratura soprano repertoire \
with a strong interest in dramatic expression and a wide \
range of musical genres.EndFragment\
\
